  "config_basis": "Task 6b, fixed before any 6b fitting and informed by the Task 6a results (a different design seed, so a different generated study and fresh confirmation settings). 6a trained every neural fit for only 400 steps and its full-tuning error stopped improving beyond 16 supplied settings, which suggests undertraining; 6b uses 3000 steps. 6a frozen-backbone tuning trained only a 192-parameter input adapter at the backbone rate and did not learn at all, so 6b gives the newly initialised 1x1 conditioner its own learning rate (identical for every neural arm) and frozen tuning additionally trains the backbone lifting and projection layers while the spectral blocks stay frozen. Unchanged from 6a: relative field loss with a floor, periodic sine/cosine coordinates, minibatch 2, cosine decay. No pilot or ablation was run for 6b; these values are choices, not tuned optima. Validation data select only each fit's saved checkpoint and the baseline ridge strength/GP kernel.",
